LP64-shaped by construction: it stuffs a function pointer through `unsigned long`, which is 32-bit on LLP64 win64 — mingw-g++ REJECTS it ("cast from pointer loses precision") while madc silently truncates and the JIT run crashes (AV at the truncated address). The win-domain-correct outcome is a compile error; unskip when madc's own pointer-to-smaller-integer diagnostic lands (KG Gap ptr_to_smaller_int_cast_diag).
